From Aqua WebKit (github.com/Wowfunhappy/WebKit, branch mavericks-backport,
AquaWebKitSupport/toolchain/patches/lld-reexport-referenced-dylib-symbols.patch, commit 11833bcc),
rebased onto 22.1.8; not yet upstream (main as of 2026-11-07 is unchanged). ld64.lld re-exports
only the dylib symbols the link references, as ld64 does.

Why: ld64.lld re-exports every dylib symbol that matches an -exported_symbols_list pattern, whether
or not the link references it. FFmpeg links each library with the pattern _av*: libavformat resolves
the libavutil symbols it uses through libavcodec's re-exports, yet still re-exported three libavutil
symbols nothing referenced. -dead_strip_dylibs (clang.cfg) then dropped libavformat's libavutil load
command, and those export-trie entries kept library ordinal 0, which names no dylib; dyldinfo
-export crashed reading them. ld64 makes a pattern-matched proxy atom global only when the link
resolved it, and literal -exported_symbol names stay re-exported here too: the driver adds them as
undefined symbols before resolution, which references them.

tests/reexport-referenced-test.sh is the regression test. To offer upstream with patches/0002.

diff --git a/lld/MachO/Driver.cpp b/lld/MachO/Driver.cpp
--- a/lld/MachO/Driver.cpp
+++ b/lld/MachO/Driver.cpp
@@ -1662,7 +1662,11 @@
           defined->privateExtern = true;
         }
       } else if (auto *dysym = dyn_cast<DylibSymbol>(sym)) {
-        dysym->shouldReexport = config->exportedSymbols.match(sym->getName());
+        // Re-export a dylib symbol only when the link references it, as ld64
+        // does: an unreferenced one can come from a dylib -dead_strip_dylibs
+        // then drops, leaving an export-trie entry with no library ordinal.
+        dysym->shouldReexport = dysym->isReferenced() &&
+                                config->exportedSymbols.match(sym->getName());
       }
     });
     if (warningsCount > kMaxWarnings)
